  NOT A READOUT: whether a crossing appears at BLOCK_M=16. On the H200 band both worlds say none does (160.0 against ridge 142.7973479416667 is 12.0% of headroom), so the presence or absence of one separates nothing there. How CLOSE the tile gets is the readout, and that is C1.  NOTE: at THIS band's low end 142.7973479416667 the retracted ceiling 160.0 is ABOVE the ridge, so on this card the retracted world does predict a crossing and its absence is informative as well.
  NOT A PRODUCTION CLAIM: vLLM ran BLOCK_M=16 multi-tile in ISOLATED CELLS: 1 of 24 observed cells on the padded count (load_max_rows), 1 of 168 seed-rows, up to 2 M-tiles per expert; on mean rows 0 of 24 cells, up to 1 tile. Q(n) = 1 everywhere else, so this ceiling is reached for in production only there and never as a regime. This run tests the CAP FORMULA at this tile height. BLOCK_M=128 is the regime that carries the production claim and scripts/bm128_depth.py is where it is asked.
  NOT RUN: the parent sweep's gate 3 (the fitted alpha's interval against ALPHA_BAND [0.529, 0.588] in BOTH directions; its retired one-sided 0.33 threshold is printed there, not scored) is superseded here by C2, which fits the same re-read fraction and then does the thing the cap claim needs: converts it to a ceiling, prints the EXA factor that ceiling is high by, and compares it with the ridge.

MINIMUM DETECTABLE EFFECT, from ONE stated assumption and no other
  assumed per-cell relative timing spread 1.50% (--plant-noise; the published H200 ladders run 0.76-1.82% and the A100 ones 0.48-0.61%, so the default 1.50% is near the top of the range a gate has to survive, not a floor)
  two-sided 5% at 80% power throughout, which is the convention every MDE in this repository uses
  C1  peak roof fraction, ONE cell against a registered threshold: MDE 4.20% relative = 0.0079 of the roof at the refit world's predicted ceiling 0.188. The discriminating threshold 0.617 sits 54x that away, and the retracted world's ceiling 1.046 sits 109x away. C1 is not the gate that runs out of power
  C2  cap/ridge from an alpha fitted over 69 treads: the slope's relative sd is 0.405% (heteroscedastic OLS, sd_i = spread x t_i), so the cap's is 0.179% and the MDE is 0.008% relative = 1.41e-05 of the ridge. The discriminator sits 30448x that away. THIS IS THE OPTIMISTIC END and is stated as one: it assumes every tread is on the memory branch and the two-line model is exactly right, so it bounds the TIMING noise and not the model error, which at this tile height is what actually limits the fit
  V2  flatness, a RATIO OF TWO SINGLE CELLS and so sqrt(2) times the per-cell spread: MDE 5.94%, against a gate of max(2%, 3 x spread) = 4.50%. THE GATE IS INSIDE ITS OWN MDE at this spread: a true gain between 4.50% and 5.94% would be missed more often than not. That is why V2 REFUSES (UNDECIDED) once 3 x spread passes 10% instead of widening further
