READING IT. BLOCK_M=16 was swept to 132 tiles (2112 rows per expert), reached 10.2% of ridge x bandwidth, and its own ladder puts its AI ceiling at 11.2 Op/B against a ridge of 152.9. The cap formula holds at this tile height, and the depth in V4 is what makes that an exclusion rather than a shrug. WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY: that a shipped kernel is stuck below its roof. vLLM ran BLOCK_M=16 multi-tile in ISOLATED CELLS: 1 of 24 observed cells on the padded count (load_max_rows), 1 of 168 seed-rows, up to 2 M-tiles per expert; on mean rows 0 of 24 cells, up to 1 tile. Q(n) = 1 everywhere else, so this ceiling is reached for in production only there and never as a regime. BLOCK_M=128 is the multi-tile regime and scripts/bm128_depth.py is where the production reading is settled.
